Specification Test honesty
Description Decision 19, after Ken Pugh's AlignThree Spectables. Every finding here is reported only and moves no score.

Entity Finding
| Attribute | Type    | Default | Notes                         |
| Path      | String  |         | relative to the audited root  |
| Line      | Integer | 0       | one-based                     |
| Check     | String  |         | which rule produced it        |

BusinessRule Skipped tests
Description A skip marker in a test file is reported; the same text elsewhere, or quoted, is not.
Examples: SkipInput
| File              | Line text                     | Reported |
| tests/test_a.py   | @pytest.mark.skip             | yes      |
| tests/test_a.py   | @pytest.mark.xfail            | yes      |
| src/a.test.js     | test.todo('renders');         | yes      |
| src/app.py        | @pytest.mark.skip             | no       |
| tests/test_a.py   | note = '@pytest.mark.skip'    | no       |

BusinessRule Computed expectations
Description A Python test comparison whose expected value is arithmetic on variables, beside a call, is reported.
Examples: ExpectationInput
| Assertion                                | Reported | Why                                   |
| assert add(a, b) == a + b                | yes      | the expectation re-does the work      |
| assert add(2, 3) == 5                    | no       | the value is stated                   |
| assert minutes(2) == 2 * 60              | no       | arithmetic on literals is stated      |
| assert locate(p) == p / name             | no       | a path join, not arithmetic           |
| assert single == plain + 1               | no       | a relation between two results        |

BusinessRule Spectables authoring checks
Description Where a repository keeps .spectable files, three mistakes from the published grammar are reported. Unknown types are not, because no list of built-in types is published.
Examples: SpecInput
| Specification content                          | Check               | Reported |
| a row with fewer cells than its first row      | column-count        | yes      |
| a cell =Missing with no Define named Missing   | undefined-reference | yes      |
| a cell =TBR declared by a bare Define table    | undefined-reference | no       |
| two scenarios named Add items in one file      | duplicate-scenario  | yes      |
| a table inside a docstring                     | column-count        | no       |
